WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.320
So copernicium, or copernicium as the discoverers
would

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:09.010
prefer it to be pronounced, is the latest
name to go up on the

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:13.750
periodic table and it is really very exciting
because it is the

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.050
first time in as many years that a new name
has appeared.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.330
And not only has it appeared but quite excitingly,
it has

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.449
appeared with a bit of controversy - what
should the symbol

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:28.039
be? The first suggestion was that it should
be called, the

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:34.260
symbol should be Cp, capital C with little
p and that has got

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:41.050
really quite an argument inorganic chemists
who use organic

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:46.499
groups in their compounds got quite excited
because Cp is

00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:50.379
the symbol that is used for cyclopentadienyl
ion which binds

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:54.989
to all sorts of different metals and then
it was discovered or

00:00:54.989 --> 00:01:00.989
realised that, many, many years ago, Cp was
used as an

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:06.110
alternative symbol for element number 71,
lutetium, which in

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:11.580
some countries we called cassiopeium. And
I’ve looked in lots

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.290
and lots of books that I have got at home
and I can’t find one

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:19.020
of them that uses this name, but the reason
why it is

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.690
important is because now more and more old
papers, old

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:28.590
books are being digitised on the internet,
if you start

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:34.860
searching for the symbol Cp it will start
throwing up old

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.820
papers and cause confusion. So the decision
has been made

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.250
by the International Union of Pure and Applied
Chemistry or

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.810
the recommendation is that the symbol should
be Cn, capital

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:52.710
C, little n. And I think that this is a very
sensible suggestion

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.340
because it is unlikely that it can be confused
with cyanide

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:01.380
which is capital C, capital N. And it is also
nice for our Chinese

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.280
colleagues because Cn is the domain name for
Chinese

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.989
websites and I think most chemists will be
very happy with

00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:11.989
that.

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:17.040
The element itself was first made quite a
few years ago, and

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.420
it’s made like all these heavy elements
by taking the nuclei of

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:26.290
two atoms that are lighter and banging them
together and if

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.879
you are aiming for element 112 then you need
to take 2

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:35.779
nuclei, which have atomic numbers which when
you add them

00:02:35.779 --> 00:02:42.459
together come up to 112, so in this case you
take lead which

00:02:42.459 --> 00:02:48.930
is atomic number 82 and so to get from 82
to 112 you need

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:54.879
to add 30, so you accelerate zinc atoms which
have atomic

00:02:54.879 --> 00:03:01.269
number of 30 towards these in a high speed
accelerator and

00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:06.819
every so often, and quite rarely, these two
nuclei fuse

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:13.279
together to give you an element or an atom
of element 112.

00:03:13.279 --> 00:03:18.510
When you make the atom, it exists, for a short
time which

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.450
might be a thousandth of a second, or a few
thousandths of a

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.520
second or it might be as long as half a second
or even a

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:32.189
second. And then the nucleus of the atom starts
to decay.

00:03:32.189 --> 00:03:36.439
Now it doesn’t blow into parts which are
just protons and

00:03:36.439 --> 00:03:41.150
neutrons in one great whoosh! But instead
it starts going

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.760
down by steps, usually the atomic number changes
by two

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:51.860
units or one unit depending what sort of particle
is ejected

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:56.309
from the nucleus. So in the case of 112, and
I don’t know the

00:03:56.309 --> 00:04:01.360
details yet, it will decay. For example, the
first step may be

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:08.109
going from 112 to 110 then the second step
may be just one

00:04:08.109 --> 00:04:13.909
unit to 109, and then two down to 107 and
so on. Until you

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:17.360
get to an element below the mass of uranium
the mass of 92

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.160
- which is stable.

